  </div>

  <div class="insight-box">
    Crude oil prices have risen from ${first_price:.2f}/bbl in {first_date.strftime('%B %Y')} to ${last_price:.2f}/bbl in {last_date.strftime('%B %Y')}, achieving a compound annual growth rate of {cagr*100:.2f}%. The all-time high of ${max_price:.2f} was recorded in {max_date.strftime('%B %Y')}, while the minimum of ${min_price:.2f} occurred in {min_date.strftime('%B %Y')}. The dataset reveals multiple structural regime changes driven by geopolitical crises, demand shocks, and shifts in production dynamics.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- LONG-TERM TREND -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
