    1980: f"Prices peaked at ~$40 in early 1980 before a long decline driven by demand destruction, non-OPEC supply growth, and Saudi Arabia's decision to defend market share. The 1986 crash saw prices fall from ~$27 to under $10 in mid-1986 — a collapse of over 60% in six months.",
